<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Quote-only mode on the PRODUCT PAGE: remove Add to Cart.

  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING EITHER FILE — the coupling that has bitten two other platforms
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The same feature in the WooCommerce plugin nearly shipped a storefront with NO way to
  transact: its quote button hung off a hook that only fires INSIDE the add-to-cart form, so
  removing the cart button would silently have removed the quote button too. In the
  PrestaShop module the theme wraps the CTA hook in `{if !$configuration.is_catalog}`, with
  the same result. So before removing anything here, Magento's equivalent coupling was
  checked against 2.4.8 source, and the finding is recorded rather than assumed:

    - Our CTA block `tackquote.request.quote` is a child of the CONTAINER
      `product.info.main` (view/frontend/layout/catalog_product_view.xml in this module).
    - The blocks removed below live in a DIFFERENT parent: `product.info.addtocart` is a
      child of `product.info.form.content`
      (vendor/magento/module-catalog/view/frontend/layout/catalog_product_view.xml:72), and
      `product.info.addtocart.additional` is a child of
      `product.info.options.wrapper.bottom` (same file, line 86).
    - `remove="true"` unsets the named element. It does not touch other containers, and it
      does not touch a block whose only relationship to the removed one was an ordering
      hint: Magento\Framework\View\Layout\Data\Structure::reorderChildElement() reads the
      sibling's parent (Structure.php:122) and simply returns when the parents differ
      (Structure.php:130).

  So the CTA survives. Test/Unit/Layout/QuoteOnlyLayoutTest.php asserts that structurally —
  that the block this module adds is never one of the blocks it removes, and that its parent
  container is not one of theirs — so a future edit that moves the CTA under
  `product.info.form.content` (where removing the form WOULD take it with it) fails the
  suite instead of shipping.

  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  BOTH blocks must go. They render the SAME template
  (Magento_Catalog::product/view/addtocart.phtml); `product.info.addtocart.additional` is the
  copy shown for products that have custom options. Removing only the first leaves a working
  Add to Cart button on every configurable and customisable product — which the server would
  then refuse, producing precisely the "broken shop" impression this mode exists to avoid.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <referenceBlock name="product.info.addtocart" remove="true"/>
        <referenceBlock name="product.info.addtocart.additional" remove="true"/>
    </body>
</page>
